{
  "unit": {
    "id": "7",
    "title": "Asking questions",
    "blurb": "-ne questions, and \"What do you…?\"",
    "intro": "To turn a statement into a yes/no question, add _-ne_ to the first word: _Edisne pānem?_ (Do you eat bread?). English needs 'do' or 'does'; Latin does not. To ask 'what?', use _quid_, and answer with the object: _Quid edis? Pānem edō._ Notice that the question uses the 'you' form (_edis_) and the answer the 'I' form (_edō_)."
  },
